# Sync gates (pointer)

State drift is the number one workflow pain. Enforcement is now layered (Wave: always-on restructure):

| Layer | Mechanism | What |
|---|---|---|
| Inline capture | `ba-context-capture` (every turn) | New facts/decisions → SESSION-CONTEXT.md, silent |
| Deterministic breakpoints | `stop` + `preCompact` hooks (`stop-sync-check.sh`, `snapshot-before-compact.sh`) | Unpromoted-item count + staleness computed from files, injected only when real |
| Judgement breakpoints | This pointer | The triggers below — run the procedure from the reference |

**Triggers that MUST run a quick sync check:** after a debrief completes · before switching initiatives · before any Confluence publish · on `/validate-state` (report-only) · on `/wrap` (fix + close).

**Procedures** (check steps, sync card format, auto-promotion rules, action runthrough): load `references/sync-procedures.md` when a trigger fires or a sync command runs. Canonical file hierarchy on conflict: tracker > status-data > SESSION-CONTEXT > everything else (full ownership table: `ba-assistant/SKILL.md → Canonical ownership`).

`/sync-check` is retired — treat as `/validate-state`.
